s are still stopped\n  after the configured inactivity period.\n- The exposure introduces no private-API dependency for console consumers\n  (Kubernetes API only).\n- If the last-activity data is already found to be readable on a\n  console-accessible Kubernetes surface, this epic reduces to validating and\n  documenting that access path — the acceptance criteria above still must be\n  demonstrably met.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P1, data-source side): provides the \"sourced from the notebook\n  controller's activity tracking\" data that the per-project idle-workbench\n  report requires.\n"}}],"model":"zai-org/GLM-5.3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":65172,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-82c55a3249bf38e3","agent_id":"a08704833be2ccb20","session_id":"7da9b899-2570-4f45-9105-189f12061fa7","uuid":"1360ffaf-d94c-49b7-8558-e2c30807f6ad","timestamp":"2026-10-09T12:38:16.498Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9016 into epics"}
