{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bc84a2687303266f","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9016-E001\n3\ttitle: Expose workbench last-activity data for console consumption\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9016\n5\tcomponent: Notebooks\n6\tteam: Workbenches\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 0\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 0\n15\t  external_dependency: 1\n16\t  human_process_gates: 1\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Expose workbench last-activity data for console consumption\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThe notebook controller already tracks per-workbench last-activity timestamps\n34\t(used by the idle culler), but that data is collected through Jupyter server\n35\tAPI probes and is not available on a surface the web console can read — the\n36\tconsole consumes the Kubernetes API only and uses no private component APIs.\n37\tThis epic makes the controller's existing last-activity data readable through\n38\tthe Kubernetes API so per-project idle-workbench reporting can be built in the\n39\tconsole without new data collection and without private API access.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Make the per-workbench last-activity data that the notebook controller\n44\t  already collects readable through the Kubernetes API, in a form that\n45\t  per-project reporting can consume. The exact surface is an implementation\n46\t  decision for the Workbenches team.\n47\t- Cover every workbench in a project, per project.\n48\t- No change to how activity is collected (the existing probe-based tracking\n49\t  stays as-is; only its exposure changes).\n50\t- No change to culling behavior: the idle culler continues to act on the same\n51\t  activity data.\n52\t\n53\t## Acceptance Criteria\n54\t\n55\t- Given a project containing workbenches, the per-workbench last-activity data\n56\t  tracked by the notebook controller is readable through the Kubernetes API for\n57\t  every workbench in that project.\n58\t- The exposed last-activity values are consistent with the notebook\n59\t  controller's activity tracking (the same view of activity the idle culler\n60\t  acts on).\n61\t- Existing idle-culling behavior is unaffected: workbenches are still stopped\n62\t  after the configured inactivity period.\n63\t- The exposure introduces no private-API dependency for console consumers\n64\t  (Kubernetes API only).\n65\t- If the last-activity data is already found to be readable on a\n66\t  console-accessible Kubernetes surface, this epic reduces to validating and\n67\t  documenting that access path — the acceptance criteria above still must be\n68\t  demonstrably met.\n69\t\n70\t## HLR Traceability\n71\t\n72\t- HLR-1 (P1, data-source side): provides the \"sourced from the notebook\n73\t  controller's activity tracking\" data that the per-project idle-workbench\n74\t  report requires.\n75\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a5ea85c2d25cdaf4","agent_id":"a7f8fb6499b6cf050","session_id":"7da9b899-2570-4f45-9105-189f12061fa7","uuid":"9094c1d7-1602-41f7-b737-48dff3fb9250","timestamp":"2026-10-09T12:43:41.681Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bc84a2687303266f","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9016 decomposition"}
