{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a073558a16388e36","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9016-E002\n3\ttitle: Expose stale pipeline-run metadata for console consumption\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9016\n5\tcomponent: Data Science Pipelines\n6\tteam: RHOAI Pipelines\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 0\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 0\n15\t  external_dependency: 0\n16\t  human_process_gates: 1\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 4\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Expose stale pipeline-run metadata for console consumption\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tKubeflow Pipelines retains run completion metadata and per-run artifacts, and\n34\tpipeline runs are surfaced in the console today — but the console consumes the\n35\tKubernetes API only, and the per-run completion-age and retained-artifact\n36\tinformation needed to identify stale, reclaimable runs is not established on a\n37\tconsole-readable surface. This epic makes that stale-run data available through\n38\tthe Kubernetes API so per-project stale-run reporting can be built in the\n39\tconsole.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Make per-run completion time and retained-artifact information from\n44\t  Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata readable through the Kubernetes API, per\n45\t  project. The exact surface is an implementation decision for the RHOAI\n46\t  Pipelines team.\n47\t- Read-only exposure of existing metadata: no change to run execution, run\n48\t  completion handling, metadata retention, or artifact storage.\n49\t- Cover completed runs, including whether artifacts are still retained for\n50\t  each.\n51\t\n52\t## Acceptance Criteria\n53\t\n54\t- Given a project containing completed pipeline runs, per-run completion time\n55\t  and retained-artifact information is readable through the Kubernetes API for\n56\t  that project.\n57\t- The exposed data matches Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata.\n58\t- Pipeline execution, existing run listing in the console, and artifact\n59\t  retention are unaffected (read-only exposure).\n60\t- If the required stale-run data is already found to be readable on a\n61\t  console-accessible Kubernetes surface, this epic reduces to validating and\n62\t  documenting that access path — the acceptance criteria above still must be\n63\t  demonstrably met.\n64\t\n65\t## HLR Traceability\n66\t\n67\t- HLR-2 (P1, data-source side): provides the \"sourced from Kubeflow Pipelines\n68\t  run metadata\" data that the stale pipeline-run report requires.\n69\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a5ea85c2d25cdaf4","agent_id":"a7f8fb6499b6cf050","session_id":"7da9b899-2570-4f45-9105-189f12061fa7","uuid":"38487c1e-163d-4936-b905-9f6017813199","timestamp":"2026-10-09T12:43:42.216Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a073558a16388e36","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9016 decomposition"}
